<title>INDIA: India M3 money supply rises to 16.8 pct on June 20.</title>
<headline>India M3 money supply rises to 16.8 pct on June 20.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's year-on-year M3 money supply growth was 16.8 percent on June 20, up from 16.6 percent on June 6, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.  </p>
<p>		   M3 MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH (yr-on-yr in pct)</p>
<p>		   June 20,1997   June 6, 1997  June 21, 1996</p>
<p>		   16.8	     16.6	    15.5</p>
<p>Money supply was 7,295.72 billion rupees against 7,258.53 billion rupees on June 6 and 6,232.19 billion on June 21, 1996, the RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
